# Technical stack

Core Language

- TypeScript: The entire project, including frontend, backend, and shared
    packages, is written in TypeScript.

Monorepo Management

- Turborepo: Used for managing the monorepo, running tasks, and optimizing
    builds.
- pnpm: The package manager used for the workspace.

Backend & Services

- Convex: The primary backend platform. It provides the database, serverless
    functions (queries, mutations, actions), and real-time data synchronization.
- Clerk: Used for user authentication across both web and native applications.
- OpenAI API: Integrated for AI-powered features like text summarization.

Web Application (apps/web)

- Framework: Next.js 15 (using the App Router).
- UI Library: React 19.
- Styling: Tailwind CSS v4.
- UI Components: A combination of custom components, Radix UI primitives
    (e.g., Avatar, DropdownMenu), and Headless UI.

Native Application (apps/native)

- Framework: React Native managed with Expo.
- UI Library: React 19.
- Navigation: React Navigation (for stack and tab navigation).
- Styling: Standard React Native styling, likely with some utility libraries.